Package: emberdays
Title: Explore Hot Days in Australian Bushfire Seasons
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Gaurav", "Warke", , "gauravwarke8@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides daily maximum temperatures from the Australian
    Bureau of Meteorology for seven Australian cities from 1910 to 2019,
    functions that count very hot days in each bushfire season (September
    to February) and compare an early period with a recent one, and a
    Shiny app that helps residents of bushfire-prone areas check whether
    hot fire-season days have become more common where they live.
